    "result_text": "All 29 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the per-city capacity rule for owner creation in the Spring PetClinic REST app. When an owner's city already contains 50 or more owners, the create request is now rejected with **409 Conflict**.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`CityCapacityException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` in the `rest.advice` package, mirroring the existing `DuplicateTelephoneException` / `DuplicateHouseholdException` pattern.\n\n2. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `CityCapacityException` that returns a `409 Conflict` `ProblemDetail`, plus the corresponding error-detail constant.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`:\n   - Added a `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 50` constant.\n   - Added a check (alongside the other conflict checks) that throws `CityCapacityException` when `countOwnersInCity(...) >= 50`.\n   - Added a `countOwnersInCity` helper that counts existing owners with a matching city, using the same case-insensitive / whitespace-collapsed normalization (`normalizeForComparison`) already used by the customer-code and namesake logic.\n\nThe pre-existing `Cp18Tests` acceptance test (fill a city to exactly 50, then expect the 51st to be rejected with 409) now passes, and the full suite remains green.",
